@startuml ML_Lifecycle
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #E3F2FD
  BorderColor #1976D2
  FontSize 12
  FontColor #263238
  DiamondBackgroundColor #FFF9C4
  DiamondBorderColor #F57F17
}

title End-to-End Machine Learning Lifecycle

start

:**1. Problem Definition & Scoping**
----
* Define business objective
* Identify success metrics (KPIs)
* Determine ML problem type
  (Classification/Regression/Clustering)
* Assess feasibility and constraints
* Define project scope and timeline;

:**2. Data Collection & Acquisition**
----
* Identify data sources
  (Databases, APIs, Files, Sensors)
* Define data requirements
* Extract data from sources
* Ensure data privacy compliance
  (GDPR, HIPAA)
* Document data lineage;

:**3. Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)**
----
* Understand data structure
* Analyze data distributions
* Identify patterns and correlations
* Detect outliers and anomalies
* Visualize data insights
* Generate summary statistics;

:**4. Data Preprocessing & Cleaning**
----
* Handle missing values
  (Imputation/Deletion)
* Remove duplicates
* Fix inconsistent data
* Handle outliers
* Normalize/Standardize formats
* Address data quality issues;

:**5. Feature Engineering**
----
* Create new features
* Transform existing features
  (Log, Polynomial, Binning)
* Encode categorical variables
  (One-Hot, Label, Target Encoding)
* Scale/Normalize numerical features
* Feature selection/reduction
  (PCA, Feature Importance);

:**6. Data Splitting**
----
* Split into Train/Validation/Test sets
  (e.g., 70%/15%/15%)
* Apply stratification if needed
* Ensure temporal ordering
  (for time-series)
* Create cross-validation folds;

:**7. Model Selection**
----
* Identify candidate algorithms
  (Linear Models, Tree-based,
   Neural Networks, etc.)
* Consider problem constraints
  (Interpretability, Speed, Accuracy)
* Review similar problem solutions
* Select baseline models;

:**8. Model Training**
----
* Configure model parameters
* Fit model on training data
* Apply regularization techniques
  (L1/L2, Dropout)
* Handle class imbalance
  (SMOTE, Class Weights)
* Track training metrics
* Save model checkpoints;

repeat
  :**9. Model Evaluation**
  ----
  * Test on validation set
  * Calculate performance metrics
    (Accuracy, Precision, Recall,
     F1-Score, AUC-ROC, RMSE)
  * Analyze confusion matrix
  * Check for overfitting/underfitting
  * Perform error analysis
  * Compare with baseline;

  if (Model Performance\nAcceptable?) then (No)
    :**10. Hyperparameter Tuning**
    ----
    * Grid Search
    * Random Search
    * Bayesian Optimization
    * Cross-validation
    * Update parameters;
    
    :**Return to Model Training**;
  else (Yes)
  endif
repeat while (Need More Tuning?) is (Yes)
->No;

:**11. Final Model Validation**
----
* Test on held-out test set
* Verify generalization
* Document final metrics
* Perform bias/fairness analysis
* Validate business requirements;

if (Production Ready?) then (No)
  :Review Requirements\nand Restart Process;
  stop
else (Yes)
endif

:**12. Model Deployment**
----
* Choose deployment strategy
  (Batch/Real-time/Edge)
* Containerize model (Docker)
* Set up serving infrastructure
  (REST API, gRPC)
* Implement A/B testing
* Deploy to production
* Configure load balancing;

repeat
  :**13. Model Monitoring**
  ----
  * Track prediction performance
  * Monitor data drift
  * Monitor concept drift
  * Log predictions and actuals
  * Set up alerts for anomalies
  * Monitor system resources
    (Latency, Throughput)
  * Track business metrics;

  if (Model Degradation\nDetected?) then (Yes)
    :**14. Model Retraining**
    ----
    * Collect new data
    * Retrain with updated data
    * Validate new model
    * Update deployment;
  else (No)
  endif
repeat while (Continue Monitoring?) is (Yes)
->No;

legend right
  |= **ML Lifecycle Stages** |
  | 1. Problem Definition |
  | 2. Data Collection |
  | 3. EDA |
  | 4. Data Preprocessing |
  | 5. Feature Engineering |
  | 6. Data Splitting |
  | 7. Model Selection |
  | 8. Model Training |
  | 9. Model Evaluation |
  | 10. Hyperparameter Tuning |
  | 11. Final Validation |
  | 12. Deployment |
  | 13. Monitoring |
  | 14. Retraining (Continuous) |
endlegend

note right
  **Key Success Factors:**
  * Clear problem definition
  * Quality data
  * Rigorous validation
  * Continuous monitoring
  * Iterative improvement
end note

@enduml
